{
  "id": "rate-state-stable-sliding-third-science",
  "name": "Dieterich-Ruina aging friction under quasistatic spring loading",
  "description": "Contact healing and velocity/state friction feed back through quasistatic elastic loading. Stable stiffness exceeds critical(b-a)/Dc. This massless positive-sliding model excludes inertia, velocity reversal, pore-pressure change and earthquake rupture propagation. Illustrative a0.01,b0.015,stiffness/normalstress0.02 per metre,Dc1m,load/reference speed1m/s,initial V0.8m/s and age1.1s. Log-speed formulation is our algebraic variable choice; horizon30s,RK4step0.01s. Not a fault-specific or laboratory fit. Original mathematical transcription/adaptation; not a calibrated forecast. Signed net-rate flows implement the stated equations. No numerical clamps or hidden resets.",
  "category": "physics",
  "source": "https://doi.org/10.1029/JB088iB12p10359",
  "reference": "Ruina (1983), Slip instability and state variable friction laws, JGR88:10359-10370; aging/slowness law and massless spring-slider stability. Dieterich (1979), doi:10.1029/JB084iB05p02161. Explicit aging-law form also verified against Pipping (2019), Eq3.1, doi:10.1002/zamm.201800263.",
